{"agent":"fleet-verifybugs","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The changed branch directly above asserts the new contract — \"Never silent: every could-not-run names its reason, and what would let it run\" — and `could_not_run_text` now promises to append \" -- to fix: <remedy>\". But the very next return, which is also labelled `could-not-run`, does not attach a `remedy`:\n\n    return \"could-not-run\", {**ev, \"reason\": f\"unrecognized verification status {status!r}\"}\n\nInput that demonstrates it: `G.verify_regression_test` returns a status the mapping does not recognise (e.g. a status added to the gates package, or any value that falls through the `if` chain), so `_regression_status` reaches this line. `ev` then has `reason` (\"unrecognized verification status 'X'\") but no `remedy` and no fallback to `_REMEDY`, because the defaulting only happens inside the `G.REGRESSION_COULD_NOT_RUN` branch. `could_not_run_text` therefore produces only the reason; the CLI prints `[could-not-run]\\n  could not check: unrecognized verification status 'X'` with no \"to fix:\", i.e. exactly the \"gave no reason/next step\" complaint Bf144280340 is about is only half-closed for this path. The fix is to route this return through the same defaulting (`{**ev, \"reason\": ..., \"remedy\": ev.get(\"remedy\") or _REMEDY}`) as the branch above.","digest":"d9260742311a215f","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py:424 (the fallback `return \"could-not-run\", ...` in `_regression_status`)","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py:424 (the fallback `return \"could-not-run\", ...` in `_regression_status`)"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":6886,"diff_sha":"acb8f01a21076ebf63868f5b0f65f037e5151df8d925bf00ad56cac971923c65","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":217.2,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"aa35cc7b48a31b53","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bf144280340.critic.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261016T122739Z-cdaf4b52.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"4dba00ca63513b321ddbf80d57bc53cd87abb52b","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py:424 (the fallback `return \"could-not-run\", ...` in `_regression_status`)"],"tree_sha":"0ea3276ca2ae+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e5dd5b222a11fd209789637be","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":69218,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-Bf144280340","ts":"2026-10-16T12:31:17.248750Z"}
{"agent":"fleet-verifybugs","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_regression_status` ends with `return \"could-not-run\", {**ev, \"reason\": f\"unrecognized verification status {status!r}\"}`. This path produces the same `\"could-not-run\"` status the CLI now special-cases, so `could_not_run_text` is invoked on an `ev` that has no `\"remedy\"` key (unlike the two `_verify_regression` early returns and unlike the `G.REGRESSION_COULD_NOT_RUN` branch, which sets `_REMEDY`). Given e.g. a gates status string that is not one of the constants (`G.verify_regression_test` returns `\"skipped-dirty-tree\"` or any future constant), the record carries `regression_verified == \"could-not-run\"` and `regression_verify == {\"reason\": \"unrecognized verification status 'skipped-dirty-tree'\"}`; `could_not_run_text` then returns just that reason with no `\" -- to fix: ...\"` suffix, so the user is told why it did not run but not what would let it run — the exact half of the fix's stated contract (\"Never silent: every could-not-run names its reason, and what would let it run\") that this branch omits. Reusing `ev.get(\"remedy\") or _REMEDY` in the fallback (or routing it through the same branch) would make the contract hold for every status.","digest":"c1b405f4dd35d283","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py:424 (`_regression_status` fallback)","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bug_close.py:424 (`_regression_status` fallback)"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":6886,"diff_sha":"acb8f01a21076ebf63868f5b0f65f037e5151df8d925bf00ad56cac971923c65","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":244.5,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"85c4b7e8836c4aa0","output_file":".ddflow